<reference id="_headingh2vvxqiemfh8b" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 2 — Graphical Task</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a numbered procedure where the author has placed an &lt;img&gt; element with a &lt;figcaption&gt;</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>button</keyword>
        <keyword>power</keyword>
        <keyword>Power</keyword>
        <keyword>inside</keyword>
        <keyword>Locate</keyword>
        <keyword>Graphical</keyword>
        <indexterm>button</indexterm>
        <indexterm>power</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Power</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider a numbered procedure where the author has placed an <codeph>&lt;img&gt;</codeph> element with a <codeph>&lt;figcaption&gt;</codeph> inside a <codeph>&lt;figure&gt;</codeph> inside an <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> element — for example, to show a button as part of a step.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Graphical Task</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;h2 id="locate-the-power-button">Locate the Power Button&lt;/h2>
&lt;ol>
  &lt;li>
    Locate the power button.
    &lt;figure>
      &lt;img src="media/power_button.png" alt="Power button"/>
      &lt;figcaption>
        Power button location
      &lt;/figcaption>
    &lt;/figure>
  &lt;/li>
&lt;/ol></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;task id="locate_the_power_button">
  &lt;title>Locate the Power Button&lt;/title>
  &lt;taskbody>
    &lt;steps>
      &lt;step>
        &lt;cmd>Locate the power button.&lt;/cmd>
        &lt;info>
          &lt;fig>
            &lt;title>Power button location&lt;/title>
            &lt;image href="media/power_button.png">
              &lt;alt>Power button&lt;/alt>
            &lt;/image>
          &lt;/fig>
        &lt;/info>
      &lt;/step>
    &lt;/steps>
  &lt;/taskbody>
&lt;/task></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> The converter maps the <codeph>&lt;figure&gt;</codeph> and <codeph>&lt;figcaption&gt;</codeph> inside the <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> to a <codeph>&lt;fig&gt;</codeph> structure, placed inside <codeph>&lt;step&gt;&lt;info&gt;</codeph>, not inside <codeph>&lt;cmd&gt;</codeph>. The task body remains a single contiguous <codeph>&lt;steps&gt;</codeph> block.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
